Q: How to make Eleventy correctly build SCSS while in --serve mode? A: <p>If your sass is compiling on the initial build, but not when your files change and the CLI's telling you that 11ty has noticed your file has changed... super annoying, right?</p>
<p>Here's one way to make it compile every time you change a desired scss file.</p>
<p><strong>Piggyback on the <em>eleventy.beforeWatch</em> event to capture the changed file and then tell 11ty to do whatever you need done.</strong></p>
<h2>Example</h2>
<p>In the example below, a conditional checks whether the changed file ends in '.scss' and if it does it compiles a scss file and writes it out as css to the desired location.</p>
<p><em>eleventy.config.js:</em></p>
<pre><code>import * as sass from &quot;sass&quot;;
import fs from &quot;node:fs&quot;;

export default async function(eleventyConfig) {
    eleventyConfig.on(&quot;eleventy.beforeWatch&quot;, async (changedFiles) =&gt; {
        // changedFiles is an array of absolute paths
        console.log(&quot;Files changed:&quot;, changedFiles);

        if (changedFiles.some(f =&gt; f.endsWith(&quot;.scss&quot;))) {
            // Run your custom logic (e.g., call an external build script)
            console.log(&quot;Scss files modified, doing something...&quot;);

            // example: compile a specific scss file
            const result = sass.compile(&quot;./src/scss/styles.scss&quot;);

            // write out the compiled result as css
            fs.writeFileSync(&quot;./dist/css/styles.css&quot;, result.css);

            // Success.
            console.log(&quot;Compiled sass. Yippee!&quot;);
        }
    });
}
</code></pre>

Q: GROUP BY column prefix and COUNT() per group with CodeIgniter&#39;s query builder A: <p>Try this will may help you,</p>

<pre><code>function get_substr() {
   $query = $this-&gt;db
        -&gt;select('LEFT(id, 2) as sub_id , COUNT(*)', FALSE)
        -&gt;from('tbSubstr')
        -&gt;group_by('sub_id')
        -&gt;get();
   return $query-&gt;result();   
}       
</code></pre>

